course: dictionary
lesson: 8734
title: A word with many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word sergeant can name a soldier, a police officer, or part of a title. «The Sergeant sent parties of stoats off to far corners of the grounds» is about a leader of soldiers, because he gives orders to a group.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Who is being ordered about? Is there a crowd of soldiers, a police car, or a fancy title like Sergeant at Arms? Those clues point to the meaning.
explain: Sergeant is a noun, so it names a person or thing. Its plural is sergeants. A soldier sergeant is above a corporal, and a police sergeant is above a constable. Ask yourself which kind of sergeant the sentence is about.
fact: A sergeant is a soldier of middle rank, above a corporal, who is in charge of a group of soldiers.
fact: A police sergeant is a police officer of the rank above a constable.
fact: In titles you may see Sergeant Major or Sergeant at Arms.
fact: «Sergeant» is a noun, and its plural is «sergeants».
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Sergeant gives orders to a group of stoats, sending them off and fetching them back.
exercise: «The Sergeant sent parties of stoats off to far corners of the grounds.» What is the Sergeant mostly doing in this sentence? | Running off to find a new home | Singing a song for the stoats | *Giving orders to a group | Sleeping in the warm
exercise: «The police sergeant asked the driver to stop.» What kind of sergeant is this? | A soldier who sings | A cook in a school kitchen | A gardener who grows roses | *A police officer, above a constable
exercise: Which phrase is a title that uses the word sergeant? | Captain of the Boat | Corporal at Sea | Constable of the Night | *Sergeant at Arms
test: «The sergeant shouted orders, and the soldiers lined up in rows.» What does sergeant mean here? | A type of cake | *A soldier in charge of a group | A sleepy animal | A flower in the garden
test: What is the correct plural of sergeant? | *sergeants | sergeanties | sergeantes | sergeant-es
exam: Jayden reads «The sergeant arrested the thief.» Which word points to police work? | the | thief | *arrested | sergeant
